  {
   "rule": "Pronouns start a sentence just like <span class='ar'>الْبَيْتُ</span> did, and the description follows in rafʿ: <span class='ar'>هُوَ</span> <span class='ar raf'>مُهَنْدِسٌ</span>. Arabic marks gender even in “you”: <span class='ar'>أَنْتَ</span> to a man, <span class='ar'>أَنْتِ</span> to a woman."
