     "en": "He's from Japan."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "p": "<span class='ar'>مِنْ</span> is a preposition, so the country after it is majrūr: <span class='ar jarr'>الْهِنْدِ</span>. It takes a fatḥa (<span class='ar'>مِنَ</span>) before <span class='ar'>الْ</span> so the two can join smoothly."
  },
  {
   "tip": "<span class='ar'>مِنْ</span> (min, from) and <span class='ar'>مَنْ</span> (man, who) look the same without vowels. That's one reason this course always shows the vowels."
  }
 ],
